<title>BRAZIL: Brazil's bankruptcy filings down 27 pct in March.</title>
<headline>Brazil's bankruptcy filings down 27 pct in March.</headline>
<dateline>SAO PAULO 1997-04-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>Defaults and bankruptcy filings in Brazil fell 17 percent and 27 percent, respectively, in March compared to the same month 1996, the Centralized Bank Services (Serasa) said.</p>
<p>Serasa, a private data bank service for banks, said debt defaults totalled 610,600 last month against 773,600 in March 1996.</p>
<p>Bankruptcy filings reached 3,414 in March, it added.</p>
<p>((-- Romina Nicaretta, Sao Paulo newsroom, 5511 248 5415))</p>
